# dotfiles-openSUSE/.gitattributes — line-ending policy for the OS-native layer.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# core/ ships its own .gitattributes, but git only applies a .gitattributes to the
# directory tree BELOW it — so the vendored copy governs core/** and nothing else.
# Every repo-owned path (bootstrap.sh, os/, install/, ssh/, wsl/, .github/) was
# unprotected until this file existed.
#
# Why this matters more here than in most repos: this tree is routinely checked out
# on Windows (\\wsl.localhost\...), where `core.autocrlf=true` is the default and is
# set GLOBALLY on at least one machine that edits it. If bootstrap.sh ever lands on
# disk with CRLF, its shebang becomes `…/env bash\r` and every fresh install dies with
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" — and CI would not catch it, because
# the lint runner checks out a normalized copy on Linux.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf`: git auto-detects text vs binary, normalizes text to LF in the
# index, and checks it out as LF on every OS. The explicit blocks below pin the
# load-bearing classes so detection is never in play for them.
# Mirrors core/.gitattributes so vendored and repo-owned paths behave identically.

# Default: normalize all detected-text files to LF in the index and on checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ── Executable + sourced shell — MUST stay LF or the shebang/sourcing breaks ───
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.zsh       text eol=lf

# ── Config / data this layer owns ─────────────────────────────────────────────
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.gitconfig text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.jsonc     text eol=lf
*.json      text eol=lf
*.md        text eol=lf
*.txt       text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
wsl/wsl.conf text eol=lf

# ── Binaries (defensive): never normalize, never diff as text ─────────────────
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.gz        binary
*.zip       binary

# ── Vendored Core: keep it out of this repo's language stats ──────────────────
# core/ is a git subtree of dotgibson/dotfiles-core and is never hand-edited here
# (see CONTRIBUTING.md + the core-integrity CI gate). linguist-vendored stops GitHub
# reporting Core's Lua/zsh as this repo's own code.
#
# Deliberately NOT marked `-diff`: suppressing core/ diffs would also hide a hand-edit
# during review, which is precisely the thing the vendoring contract exists to catch.
# core/ line endings are governed by core/.gitattributes, which applies to its subtree.
core/** linguist-vendored
